G.append({'heading': 'Notes on this edition', 'blocks': [
 bullets([
  "Sources read for this edition: Nvidia's own release, the Wall Street Journal, Axios and the Asia Business Daily for the resignation and its market day; Yahoo Finance's historical table for the official NVDA close; the statistics office's own release for the CPI, with ET for the composition; The Hindu BusinessLine and moneycontrol for the Mumbai close and the street's levels; Financial Express for the provisional flows; Reuters' settle reports (via CNA and Livemint) and Dow Jones Data Talk for oil, gold and the ten-year; the Jerusalem Post for the claimed Saudi attacks; CNBC-TV18 for the results wave; the Kremlin's own account, AP and RFE/RL for Moscow, Abu Dhabi and Dublin; AP for the frontier lawsuit; Google's own post for Hydrogen and Orchestrator; the Zigzag repository and the Hacker News front page for the builder story; ET for Desible.ai; The Hans India for the IPO filing; BSE's official bhavcopy behind every Indian price and every computed percentage.",
  "Corrections discipline: Nvidia gave no reason for the resignation, and that is the framing throughout; the reported investigation is carried once, attributed to the Journal and the Post, without detail. The intraday low in Nvidia is left unnumbered - the wires put it at nearly 12%, 13% and 14%; the 4.34% close is the verified figure. The provisional foreign-flow print is labelled provisional; GIFT Nifty is labelled an aggregator's indication. ONGC's fall is presented with its ex-dividend arithmetic, never as a verdict.",
  "Word-count method: the standing counter (wc.py) counts the fact line (excluding this sentence), the intro and every section body including rows and bullets; charts and headings are excluded. File, site and counter agree.",
 ]),
 closing(' Nothing on this page is investment advice. Verify anything load-bearing against the linked sources.'),
]})


